    <!-- Lawnchair texts that named "Lawnchair" or were not translated, rewritten for Fugueti Launcher. -->
    <string name="fg_debug_build_warning">You are using a debug build, made for development. It may contain bugs and broken features; use the release APK every day.</string>
    <string name="fg_set_default_launcher_tip">To access shortcuts and additional features, set Fugueti as your default home app</string>
    <string name="fg_restart_launcher">Restart Fugueti</string>
    <string name="fg_open_settings">Open settings</string>
    <string name="fg_dt2s_a11y_hint">To turn the screen off with a gesture, turn on the Fugueti accessibility service. Tap \"Open settings\", select \"Fugueti\" and turn on \"Use Fugueti\".\n\nFugueti uses the accessibility method `performGlobalAction` for this action. It is a sensitive permission that would allow monitoring other apps, but Fugueti is not configured for that and receives no events.</string>
    <string name="fg_recents_a11y_hint">To open the Recents screen with a gesture, turn on the Fugueti accessibility service. Tap \"Open settings\", select \"Fugueti\" and turn on \"Use Fugueti\".\n\nFugueti uses the accessibility method `performGlobalAction` for this action. It is a sensitive permission that would allow monitoring other apps, but Fugueti is not configured for that and receives no events.</string>
    <string name="fg_dt2s_admin_hint">To turn the screen off with a gesture, set Fugueti as a device admin app. Tap \"Open settings\", then tap \"Activate this device admin app\".</string>
    <string name="fg_accessibility_service_description">Fugueti needs accessibility access to run some gesture actions, such as locking the phone or opening the Recents screen, through the performGlobalAction method.\n\nFugueti does not watch any user action, although every accessibility service is granted that privilege. Every event sent by the system is discarded.</string>

